  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Restoring safe and resilient learning in flood affected areas of Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This action will help children in southern Mozambique get back to safe schools after the recent floods that hit Mozambique during the 2025-2026 rainy season. The impacts of the floods were felt stronger in parts of Gaza and Maputo provinces and Maputo City, and the school infrastructure was especially impacted. A great number of classrooms and toilets were destroyed or damaged, and learning was interrupted for tens of thousands of children. The EU will support to rebuild and/or rehabilitate safe, flood resilient classrooms, fix water and sanitation in schools, and bring in learning material so children can recover on lost learning for grades 1&#xbf;6 in a minimum of 24 schools. The results chain is structured around two mutually reinforcing specific objectives:Rehabilitate/construct classrooms to climate resilient standards, restore WASH facilities and ensure minimum safety requirements in suitable locations, andAccelerate learning recovery aligned to the national curriculum for Grades 1&#xbf;6, in the same schools The Action will target the provinces of Gaza, Maputo and Maputo City.</narrative>
  </description>
